         fhir:comment [ fhir:v "Element `Citation.citedArtifact.contributorship.entry.contributionType` is part of an existing definition because parent element `Citation.citedArtifact.contributorship.entry` requires a cross-version extension.\nElement `Citation.citedArtifact.contributorship.entry.contributionType` is not mapped to FHIR R4, since FHIR R5 `Citation` is not mapped.\nElement `Citation.citedArtifact.contributorship.entry.contributionType` has no mapping targets in FHIR R4. Typically, this is because the element has been added (is a new element).\nThe CreDiT taxonomy provides a way to encode contribution information. The purpose of CRediT is to provide transparency in contributions to scholarly published work, to enable improved systems of attribution, credit, and accountability." ]
